# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Remote Support Program
#
# Three things must never be committed: build output (large and regenerable), the staged payloads
# (~1 GB of self-contained exes), and anything secret — the tenant key, the SQLite database and
# the Data Protection keys that encrypt stored workshop passwords.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- build output ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Note: patterns are lowercase-explicit where a case-insensitive match could bite. Do NOT add a
# bare "data/" rule — on Windows git is case-insensitive by default and it would also swallow
# src/RemoteSupport.Platform/Data/, which is source (PlatformDb.cs and the EF migrations).
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
TestResults/

# ---- staged payloads (regenerate with .\build.ps1) --------------------------------------------
/dist/
/demo/

# The deploy-client folder is a hand-assembled package: keep the scripts and branding, leave out
# the 170 MB of binaries that build.ps1 produces.
/deploy-client/*.exe

# ---- secrets and live data --------------------------------------------------------------------
# brand.json carries the tenant key, which authenticates devices to a tenant. Copy it back from
# the portal, or from branding/brand.example.json, after a fresh clone.
**/branding/brand.json

# The platform's SQLite database, uploaded tenant logos, and the Data Protection keys. Losing the
# keys loses every stored workshop password, so back them up somewhere private — but not here.
**/data/keys/
**/data/logos/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Legacy single-tenant server's runtime state
/src/RemoteSupport.Server/data/

# ---- misc --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local portal credentials for the diagnostic harnesses in tools/. Never commit this.
/tools/rs-credentials.json
# The harnesses' own PostgreSQL account (tools/Setup-TestPostgres.ps1). Test-only, but a password all the same.
/tools/rs-postgres.txt
# Clint's PayFast SANDBOX account for tools/payfastcheck (tools/Save-PayfastSandbox.ps1), encrypted to this Windows user.
/tools/payfast-sandbox.xml

# Timestamped copies that tools/deploy-client-payload.ps1 keeps before editing appsettings.json.
# They are a local safety net, not source, and one of them carries whatever PublicUrl was set
# on that machine at the time.
*.bak-*

# Publish-Landing.ps1 -PreviewOnly renders the finished holding page here, phone number and
# all. It is a local preview of a generated file, never the source.
landing/preview.html

# THEME PREVIEW — tools\Preview-Theme.ps1 regenerates these from landing/index.html every run.
# Generated, never deployed, and they carry the phone number filled in.
landing/preview-dark-*.html

# Publish-Landing.ps1 -ForUpload renders the page here, named index.html, ready to put through
# konsoleH by hand. Generated from landing/index.html, so the source is the thing to edit.
landing/upload/

# Contracts and company paperwork. Anchored to the repository root and named in full, so it
# cannot catch a src/.../Legal/ folder if one is ever added. These are private documents that
# happen to sit beside the code; keep them backed up somewhere else, because git is not backing
# them up.
/legal/

# ---- the test checklist remembers where the shared drive is, per PC ----------------------------
/tools/testchecklist/share-path.txt
# Harness runs on each database (tools/Run-DbHarnesses.ps1): output, not source.
/tools/dbruns/
# Server reports (deploy/Get-ServerReport.ps1): a picture of the live server, kept locally.
/deploy/reports/
